he minor of ${a}_{11}$ is\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}p & 4 \\\\ -2 & p\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}p & 4 \\\\ -2 & p\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =p\\cdot p-4\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & ={p}^{2}+8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${a}_{11}$ is $17$, so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}^{2}+8 & =17 \\\\ {p}^{2}-9 & =0 \\\\ (p-3)(p+3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $p=-3$ and $p=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037782/state.json" "file_sha256" "38bb04d000f05b25d1e93fe0abbc555eb6432cef80f38cea471d9e2d0a1e26cc"} {"question" "q-275530" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037782/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a4dd318212df18d98a355bb767d83eb1fe8560ad809fa5462916bbfb0972d207"} {"question" "q-275530" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037782/state.json" "file_sha256" "38bb04d000f05b25d1e93fe0abbc555eb6432cef80f38cea471d9e2d0a1e26cc"} {"question" "q-275530" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037782/state.json" "file_sha256" "38bb04d000f05b25d1e93fe0abbc555eb6432cef80f38cea471d9e2d0a1e26cc"} {"question" "q-275530" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037782/state.json" "file_sha256" "38bb04d000f05b25d1e93fe0abbc555eb6432cef80f38cea471d9e2d0a1e26cc"} {"question" "q-275530" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037782/state.json" "file_sha256" "38bb04d000f05b25d1e93fe0abbc555eb6432cef80f38cea471d9e2d0a1e26cc"} {"question" "q-18239" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the minor of ${c}_{23}$ is $-86$, find all the possible values of $x$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 11 & x & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037782/state.json" "file_sha256" "38bb04d000f05b25d1e93fe0abbc555eb6432cef80f38cea471d9e2d0a1e26cc"} {"question" "q-18239" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we remove the second row and third column:\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 7 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & 5 \\\\ 11 & x & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe minor of ${c}_{23}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 7 \\\\ 11 & x\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 7 \\\\ 11 & x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot x-7\\cdot 11 \\\\  & =-3x-77.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${c}_{23}$ is $-86$, so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x-77 & =-86 \\\\ -3x & =-9 \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037782/state.json" "file_sha256" "38bb04d000f05b25d1e93fe0abbc555eb6432cef80f38cea471d9e2d0a1e26cc"} {"question" "q-18239" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037782/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a4dd318212df18d98a355bb767d83eb1fe8560ad809fa5462916bbfb0972d207"} {"question" "q-18239" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037782/state.json" "file_sha256" "38bb04d000f05b25d1e93fe0abbc555eb6432cef80f38cea471d9e2d0a1e26cc"} {"question" "q-18239" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-12"] ["math" "x=-3"] ["math" "x=-9"] ["math" "x=3"] ["math" "x=9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037782/state.json" "file_sha256" "38bb04d000f05b25d1e93fe0abbc555eb6432cef80f38cea471d9e2d0a1e26cc"} {"question" "q-18239" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037782/state.json" "file_sha256" "38bb04d000f05b25d1e93fe0abbc555eb6432cef80f38cea471d9e2d0a1e26cc"} {"question" "q-128116" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the minor of ${r}_{33}$ is $3$, find all the possible values of $z$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}z & -3 & -1 \\\\ 5 & z-8 & 8 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 6z\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037782/state.json" "file_sha256" "38bb04d000f05b25d1e93fe0abbc555eb6432cef80f38cea471d9e2d0a1e26cc"} {"question" "q-128116" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we remove the third row and third column:\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}z & -3 & ∗ \\\\ -5 & z-8 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & 6z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe minor of ${r}_{33}$ is\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}z & -3 \\\\ 5 & z-8\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}z & -3 \\\\ 5 & z-8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =z\\cdot (z-8)-(-3)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & ={z}^{2}-8z+15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${r}_{33}$ is $3$, so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{2}-8z+15 & =3 \\\\ {z}^{2}-8z+12 & =0 \\\\ (z-2)(z-6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $z=2$ and $z=6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037782/state.json" "file_sha256" "38bb04d000f05b25d1e93fe0abbc555eb6432cef80f38cea471d9e2d0a1e26cc"} {"question" "q-128116" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037782/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a4dd318212df18d98a355bb767d83eb1fe8560ad809fa5462916bbfb0972d207"} {"question" "q-128116" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037782/state.json" "file_sha256" "38bb04d000f05b25d1e93fe0abbc555eb6432cef80f38cea471d9e2d0a1e26cc"} {"question" "q-128116" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$z=-1$ only"] ["text" "$z=-4$ only"] ["text" "$z=2$ and $z=6$ only"] ["text" "$z=2$ only"] ["text" "$z=3$ and $z=6$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037782/state.json" "file_sha256" "38bb04d000f05b25d1e93fe0abbc555eb6432cef80f38cea471d9e2d0a1e26cc"} {"question" "q-128116" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$z=2$ and $z=6$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037782/state.json" "file_sha256" "38bb04d000f05b25d1e93fe0abbc555eb6432cef80f38cea471d9e2d0a1e26cc"} {"question" "e-4439" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the minor of the entry $b_{21}$ in the matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}10 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 7 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037782/example-4439.json" "file_sha256" "52f40ccd834aaab7ac53f555879411bf4897dc5b68d572af815dc32e7284b121"} {"question" "e-4439" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The minor of $b_{21} = 3$ (second row, first column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $3$ are removed: \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & 7 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of $b_{21}=3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2-5\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =2-35 \\\\  & =-33.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037782/example-4439.json" "file_sha256" "52f40ccd834aaab7ac53f555879411bf4897dc5b68d572af815dc32e7284b121"} {"question" "e-4440" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the minor of $c_{22}$ in the matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7x & 0 & -3y \\\\ 1 & x+2y & 4 \\\\ -y & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037782/example-4440.json" "file_sha256" "a5112db55b664532de0130c202c6b6e919c5c44ac143c1b3e00ea18492050162"} {"question" "e-4440" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we remove the second row and second column: \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7x & ∗ & -3y \\\\ ∗ & x+2y & ∗ \\\\ -y & ∗ & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}7x & -3y \\\\ -y & 5\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}7x & -3y \\\\ -y & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =7x\\cdot 5-(-3y)\\cdot (-y) \\\\  & =35x-3{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037782/example-4440.json" "file_sha256" "a5112db55b664532de0130c202c6b6e919c5c44ac143c1b3e00ea18492050162"} {"question" "e-4441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the minor of $a_{23}$ is $5,$ find all the possible values of $k$ in the matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 3 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 2 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 2k & -6\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037782/example-4441.json" "file_sha256" "7b0302819c882ad98b46d9e471117c6f55cf0debed9240f0e7ab4734d6d5219a"} {"question" "e-4441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we remove the second row and third column:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 3 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & 7 \\\\ -1 & 2k & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe minor of $a_{23}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2k\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k\\cdot 2k-3\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =2{k}^{2}+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of $a_{23}$ is $5,$ so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{k}^{2}+3 & =5 \\\\ 2{k}^{2} & =2 \\\\ {k}^{2} & =1 \\\\ k & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $k=-1$ and $k=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037782/example-4441.json" "file_sha256" "7b0302819c882ad98b46d9e471117c6f55cf0debed9240f0e7ab4734d6d5219a"}] "usage" {"q-127701" [] "e-4441" [] "e-4439" [] "q-1098" [] "q-128030" [] "e-4440" [] "q-275530" [] "q-319112" [] "q-275501" []} "basis" 1291 "retractions" [[17592186257814 :que